preConditionHook:
// EL: for kk = 0 to consecutiveBars - 1, sum AbsValue(close - open) over the
// bodyLookback bars ending at kk + 1, divide by bodyLookback, and require bar
// kk to be a bull bar whose body is at least bodyMultiple times that mean.
//
// At consecutiveBars = 1 this is Brooks's 'body about the same size as or
// larger than the median body of the past five or ten bars' -- the MEAN
// replaces the median deliberately: a median needs the window sorted every
// bar, the mean is a running sum, and the claim is comparative size. At
// consecutiveBars = 2 or 3 it is the follow-through run, which is why the
// count is an input rather than a second rule.
//
// The benchmark window EXCLUDES the bar it judges (bars kk+1 .. kk+bodyLookback),
// so an outsized body cannot raise its own benchmark -- the convention
// LargeOutsideBar, BarRangeBelowAverageMultiple and LargeTailedBarCount set --
// and it shifts with the counted bar, which is why the mean is an explicit
// summation rather than Average(...)[kk + 1]: a function-history reference at a
// loop-variable offset is not a registered behaviour. The summation runs
// newest-first, EasyLanguage's Summation order, and divides by the same (int)
// bound the loop uses.
//
// Average over a price EXPRESSION with real history, so a fresh loop -- not the
// WFSafe_AvgTrueRange rolling accumulator, and not a zero-filled variable
// mirror.
//
// All-of-N written the way StrongTrendBarRun writes it: start true and let any
// failing bar clear the flag, so the loop runs unconditionally and
// EasyLanguage's lack of short-circuiting cannot matter. Both sides are
// computed here for the same reason. A tie bar (close == open within the EL
// tolerance) fails both sides.
//
// The flags and the accumulators are class members and persist across bars, so
// all four are reset before use.
allBigBull = true;
allBigBear = true;
for (int k = 0; k < (int)consecutiveBars; ++k) {
    bodySum = 0.0;
    for (int j = 0; j < (int)bodyLookback; ++j) {
        bodySum = bodySum + std::fabs(close[k + 1 + j] - open[k + 1 + j]);
    }
    avgBody = bodySum / (int)bodyLookback;
    if (el_le(close[k], open[k])) allBigBull = false;
    if (el_lt(close[k] - open[k], bodyMultiple * avgBody)) allBigBull = false;
    if (el_ge(close[k], open[k])) allBigBear = false;
    if (el_lt(open[k] - close[k], bodyMultiple * avgBody)) allBigBear = false;
}
